A mode is one of opening, title, main menu, intro, naming, custom naming, rival naming, custom rival naming, walk, dialogue, starter, battle, battle party, battle bag, field menu, party, bag, trainer card, town map or shop.
An adventure has a place (text), a column (number), a row (number), a facing (text), a mode (mode), a message (text), a stage (text), an objective (text), a starter (text), a rival starter (text), a trainer (text), a rival (text), a parcel (number), a dex (number), a badge (number), a tm34 (number), a town map (number), a blue house entered (number), a daisy walking (number), a route rival beaten (number), a wallet (number), a selection (number), an animation (number) and an opponent (text).
Let the progress values always be a list of 0 and 1.
An adventure's parcel is always in the progress values.
An adventure's dex is always in the progress values.
An adventure's badge is always in the progress values.
An adventure's tm34 is always in the progress values.
An adventure's town map is always in the progress values.
An adventure's blue house entered is always in the progress values.
An adventure's daisy walking is always in the progress values.
An adventure's route rival beaten is always in the progress values.
A controller has an action (text) and a rendering (number).
A controller is ready when its action is not "".

